## Bring the energy of African drumming to your school

Rhythm Culture’s Drum Sing Dance school incursions are packed with exciting rhythmic activities, so your students will be on the edge of their seats. Through traditional West African rhythms, students connect through music, movement and sound. As a result, everyone gets involved in a lively, hands-on experience.

For example, students explore coordination, connection and musical dynamics. They also discover tempo and rhythm through the incredible sound of the djembe. Above all, our workshops are fast-paced, engaging, educational and great fun!
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Experience the culture behind the rhythms

What makes our school incursions special is the cultural knowledge our artists bring. All our facilitators have studied in West Africa, so they share personal stories, musical knowledge and first-hand experience of Africa’s diverse traditions.

As a result, students don’t just learn to play a drum or follow a dance step. Instead, they experience the culture, history and traditions behind the music.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

{% section tone="dark" %}
### Sunshine Coast school?

We’re a local team based in Palmwoods, with no travel fees anywhere on the coast.

{% button label="See our Sunshine Coast school incursions" href="/school-incursions/school-incursion-sunshine-coast/" align="center" /%}
{% /section %}

## Choose from three school incursions

Every workshop is tailored to your students’ year level and abilities. Not sure which one suits you best? In that case, we’re happy to talk it through.

{% columns layout="equal" align="top" %}
{% column %}
*Most popular*

### Drum Sing Dance

Drumming, singing and dance combined. First, students rotate through all three. Then they bring their skills together in one energetic ensemble.

**Great for:** Harmony Day, rewards days, end-of-year celebrations and whole-school events.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
*Music*

### African Drumming Workshop

Traditional West African rhythms on authentic djembes, as well as rhythm games, call-and-response and ensemble playing.

**Great for:** Music classes, Under 8s Day and cultural studies.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
*Dance & performing arts*

### African Dance Workshop

Rhythmic footwork, body percussion and dynamic West African movement. Live drumming can also be added.

**Great for:** Primary groups, as well as secondary dance students building choreography for assessment.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

